# Defect 291, 2026-10-05: an excerpt wrote a character a terminal shows as
# nothing as itself, so a no-break space, a zero-width space or a byte order
# mark on the line a message quoted showed the reader nothing to find, where
# defect 244 wrote a control character by its code. Each is written by its
# code now, `<U+00A0>`, in the excerpt and wherever a message quotes it, the
# caret padded by that width; a visible character above ASCII is shown as
# itself. Each line is a type error a string's text stands on.

function main()
    a: i64 = "a b​c"  #~ type_mismatch
    b: i64 = "﻿d"  #~ type_mismatch
    c: i64 = "café €"  #~ type_mismatch
    print(a + b + c)
